## Goal
Visualize the relationship between samples using Principal Component Analysis (PCA) of normalized gene expression counts. Generate a plot showing the first two principal components, with samples colored by treatment condition (treated vs untreated) to assess whether samples cluster by treatment status and identify any outliers.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |

## Method
1. Load the gene counts matrix (salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv) into R using the `tidyverse` and `DESeq2` packages in the `gars-bio` conda environment.
2. Filter genes with zero or near-zero counts (sum < 1 across all samples) to reduce noise.
3. Perform variance stabilizing transformation (VST) using DESeq2 on the filtered counts.
4. Perform PCA on the transformed counts using the `prcomp()` function, scaling each gene.
5. Load the design metadata (condition: treated vs untreated) from the design table.
6. Create a PCA plot showing PC1 vs PC2, with points colored by treatment condition; generate a scree plot showing variance explained by the first 10 PCs.
7. Save both plots and PC loadings/scores to results/.
8. Script runs under `Runs: batch` on the configured cluster.

